WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.064 --> 00:00:00.897
(crowd cheering)
- Okay,

00:00:00.897 --> 00:00:02.510
so it's time to introduce our first guest.

00:00:02.510 --> 00:00:03.750
And I dunno who it is.

00:00:03.750 --> 00:00:05.097
I hope they like margaritas and quesos,

00:00:05.097 --> 00:00:05.930
and if they don't,

00:00:05.930 --> 00:00:07.060
leave. (chuckling)
(crowd laughs)

00:00:07.060 --> 00:00:08.332
Please welcome the star of one

00:00:08.332 --> 00:00:10.540
of my favorite shows on television.

00:00:10.540 --> 00:00:12.361
Come on out, whoever you are.

00:00:12.361 --> 00:00:14.345
(upbeat music)

00:00:14.345 --> 00:00:15.930
(Kelly yells)

00:00:15.930 --> 00:00:20.930
(Kelly laughs)
(crowd cheers)

00:00:21.889 --> 00:00:22.972
I am so done.

00:00:34.074 --> 00:00:34.991
Oh my gosh.

00:00:36.790 --> 00:00:38.690
So basically, I'm on a date,

00:00:38.690 --> 00:00:39.550
drinking with Nathan Fillion,

00:00:39.550 --> 00:00:40.529
that's what's happening.
(crowd laughs)

00:00:40.529 --> 00:00:41.362
I'm just kidding,

00:00:41.362 --> 00:00:42.195
I'm just kidding.
- Are you surprised?

00:00:42.195 --> 00:00:43.028
- I am.

00:00:43.028 --> 00:00:44.470
I literally have nothing, no idea.

00:00:44.470 --> 00:00:46.530
- We wanted to surprise you.

00:00:46.530 --> 00:00:47.363
- Okay, okay.

00:00:47.363 --> 00:00:49.320
- But I didn't want this
to be the only surprise.

00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:50.280
- Oh, it's enough.

00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:51.322
- Can I bring some more?

00:00:51.322 --> 00:00:52.155
- Oh yeah.

00:00:52.155 --> 00:00:52.988
Oh are you?

00:00:52.988 --> 00:00:53.821
Please say, okay.

00:00:53.821 --> 00:00:55.070
- I want you guys to all welcome,

00:00:55.070 --> 00:00:57.282
please welcome, Mekia Cox.

00:00:57.282 --> 00:00:58.130
- Yes.

00:00:58.130 --> 00:01:01.143
- Alyssa Diaz, Melissa
O'Neil and Eric Winter.

00:01:01.143 --> 00:01:02.366
- Yes.
(crowd cheering)

00:01:02.366 --> 00:01:05.993
I am, I'm so excited.
(upbeat music)

00:01:05.993 --> 00:01:08.743
(crowd cheering)

00:01:11.539 --> 00:01:12.372
Oh my God.

00:01:14.865 --> 00:01:16.365
How are you doing?

00:01:19.067 --> 00:01:21.817
(crowd cheering)

00:01:23.394 --> 00:01:26.359
All right, so Vic, would you
mind running over some chips,

00:01:26.359 --> 00:01:29.673
and drinks to the entire
cast of The Rookie?

00:01:29.673 --> 00:01:31.450
(hands clapping)

00:01:31.450 --> 00:01:33.999
I'm so excited I'm sweating.

00:01:33.999 --> 00:01:34.832
(Eric and Melissa laughing)

00:01:34.832 --> 00:01:35.665
I'm sweating.

00:01:35.665 --> 00:01:36.498
I have my drink.
- Thank you,

00:01:36.498 --> 00:01:37.331
thank you very much.

00:01:37.331 --> 00:01:38.164
- [Mekia] Unfortunately, I can't.

00:01:38.164 --> 00:01:39.450
(Mekia chuckles)
- Oh my gosh, y'all,

00:01:39.450 --> 00:01:41.310
don't dive into The Rookie unless you're

00:01:41.310 --> 00:01:42.640
in for the long haul.

00:01:42.640 --> 00:01:43.473
- Hello. (chuckling)

00:01:43.473 --> 00:01:44.590
Thank you.
- [Kelly] It is so good.

00:01:44.590 --> 00:01:45.440
- [Vic] You're welcome.

00:01:45.440 --> 00:01:46.273
- [Nathan] Woo.

00:01:46.273 --> 00:01:47.660
- I got so addicted.

00:01:47.660 --> 00:01:49.300
I literally requested.

00:01:49.300 --> 00:01:50.630
I love that you did this for my birthday.

00:01:50.630 --> 00:01:52.243
I called my executive producer,

00:01:52.243 --> 00:01:53.076
(Nathan chuckling)
I was like,

00:01:53.076 --> 00:01:54.050
"Please, okay, I love Nathan,

00:01:54.050 --> 00:01:55.580
I want the whole cast."

00:01:55.580 --> 00:01:57.190
I was like, "Please get them on my show."

00:01:57.190 --> 00:01:58.930
I love that you did it for my birthday.

00:01:58.930 --> 00:02:00.230
Do y'all have so much fun with each other?

00:02:00.230 --> 00:02:01.720
'Cause I know not every set can be

00:02:01.720 --> 00:02:03.332
that magical with chemistry.

00:02:03.332 --> 00:02:04.350
- We do.

00:02:04.350 --> 00:02:05.773
We do have a lot of fun.
- We do.

00:02:05.773 --> 00:02:06.606
- And sometimes-

00:02:06.606 --> 00:02:07.439
- You're such a hardass.
- to the extent that-

00:02:07.439 --> 00:02:08.272
- I love it.

00:02:08.272 --> 00:02:09.334
(Mekia laughs)
(crowd laughs)

00:02:09.334 --> 00:02:10.310
Yes, okay, sorry, go, go.

00:02:10.310 --> 00:02:12.130
- It's up to the extent
that when we're waiting

00:02:12.130 --> 00:02:14.070
between takes and we're all hanging out,

00:02:14.070 --> 00:02:17.160
we're taking too much
time to get back to set,

00:02:17.160 --> 00:02:21.400
because we're talking, we're
laughing, we're playing games.

00:02:21.400 --> 00:02:22.270
We play a lot of games.

00:02:22.270 --> 00:02:23.120
- You play games?

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:25.230
- I feel bad for the directors,

00:02:25.230 --> 00:02:27.290
because they come in and their job is to,

00:02:27.290 --> 00:02:28.370
you know, get through the day,

00:02:28.370 --> 00:02:29.430
get through all of their scenes.

00:02:29.430 --> 00:02:30.860
But they usually have to add on,

00:02:30.860 --> 00:02:33.140
when we're all there at the same time.

00:02:33.140 --> 00:02:34.041
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:02:34.041 --> 00:02:34.920
- They have to add on an hour to the day,

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:36.920
'cause they know that we're
gonna be talking, playing games.

00:02:36.920 --> 00:02:38.340
- It can be a bit of chaos.

00:02:38.340 --> 00:02:39.335
- Yeah.
- This is kind of-

00:02:39.335 --> 00:02:40.168
- In a good way.
- They don't like scenes

00:02:40.168 --> 00:02:41.050
with us together anymore.

00:02:41.050 --> 00:02:42.870
We used to be in the roll
call room all the time.

00:02:42.870 --> 00:02:44.400
And if you notice as the seasons go,

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:45.720
we're not in there as much anymore,

00:02:45.720 --> 00:02:48.348
because we don't compare our days.

00:02:48.348 --> 00:02:49.181
(Eric and Melissa laughs)

00:02:49.181 --> 00:02:50.014
- Yes.
- Oh my God,

00:02:50.014 --> 00:02:51.490
this is like me and my
friend Mary from childhood.

00:02:51.490 --> 00:02:52.690
They separated us young.

00:02:52.690 --> 00:02:54.810
They were like, "They
won't actually shut up."

00:02:54.810 --> 00:02:57.610
So yeah but social.
(Alyssa laughs)

00:02:57.610 --> 00:02:59.780
So what are everyone's
most memorable birthdays?

00:02:59.780 --> 00:03:01.320
I'll start with you, Nathan.

00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:03.172
- My most memorable birthday,

00:03:03.172 --> 00:03:05.356
oh God, start with somebody
else, please, please.

00:03:05.356 --> 00:03:07.340
(Kelly and Alyssa laughs)

00:03:07.340 --> 00:03:09.160
- Okay, anybody right off the bat.

00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:13.260
- My favorite birthday
was when I turned 30,

00:03:13.260 --> 00:03:15.950
and my grandmother had recently passed,

00:03:15.950 --> 00:03:17.350
and I heard this word. (chuckling)

00:03:17.350 --> 00:03:18.560
Wow, I'm really going deep.

00:03:18.560 --> 00:03:20.550
I heard this word I'd never
heard before, Hyperion.

00:03:20.550 --> 00:03:21.750
And I was like, "I'm gonna look this up."

00:03:21.750 --> 00:03:24.050
And Hyperion is one of
the tallest redwood trees.

00:03:24.050 --> 00:03:26.690
And for that birthday I found it.

00:03:26.690 --> 00:03:29.490
But you have to geolocate
it and it's not on a trail.

00:03:29.490 --> 00:03:31.440
And so I was like wading
through this river.

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:33.230
Totally clear, you can see
all the way to the stones,

00:03:33.230 --> 00:03:35.300
like carrying my sack over my bag.

00:03:35.300 --> 00:03:36.210
Climbing over the redwood.
- What kind of movie

00:03:36.210 --> 00:03:37.046
are you living in right now?
(crowd chuckling)

00:03:37.046 --> 00:03:38.030
(Melissa laughs)
What?

00:03:38.030 --> 00:03:38.871
- A good one.

00:03:38.871 --> 00:03:39.880
- That's amazing.
(Melissa laughs)

00:03:39.880 --> 00:03:40.713
- It's a Saturday thing. (chuckling)

00:03:40.713 --> 00:03:42.040
- And you found it?

00:03:42.040 --> 00:03:43.230
Are you that kind of person?

00:03:43.230 --> 00:03:44.204
You're always adventurous like that?

00:03:44.204 --> 00:03:45.037
- [Alyssa] Yes.

00:03:45.037 --> 00:03:46.331
- Yeah, who doesn't love redwood trees?

00:03:46.331 --> 00:03:49.087
- I am a nerd.
- (chuckling) Eric, Eric does.

00:03:49.087 --> 00:03:50.767
I'm a total nerd.
- I love 'em, baby.

00:03:50.767 --> 00:03:52.022
(Kelly laughs)
(crowd laughs)

00:03:52.022 --> 00:03:53.078
- I'm more of a elm guy.

00:03:53.078 --> 00:03:53.911
(Melissa laughs)

00:03:53.911 --> 00:03:56.010
- Okay, now you have to
one up redwoods, Eric.

00:03:56.010 --> 00:03:56.843
- [Eric] Well, I mean, yeah.
- What's

00:03:56.843 --> 00:03:57.676
your favorite birthday?

00:03:57.676 --> 00:04:00.040
- It's on my 27th birthday.

00:04:00.040 --> 00:04:02.001
I planted a redwood tree.

00:04:02.001 --> 00:04:03.120
(Kelly and crowd laughs)

00:04:03.120 --> 00:04:03.953
And-

00:04:03.953 --> 00:04:04.786
- No, you didn't.

00:04:04.786 --> 00:04:05.619
Did you really?

00:04:05.619 --> 00:04:06.452
- So I gave back

00:04:06.452 --> 00:04:07.285
to mother earth.
- Yeah and then I turned 37

00:04:07.285 --> 00:04:08.630
I climbed it and built

00:04:09.647 --> 00:04:11.382
a house up there.
- I actually believed him

00:04:11.382 --> 00:04:12.453
when he said he planted one.

00:04:12.453 --> 00:04:14.380
And I planted another flower,

00:04:14.380 --> 00:04:16.198
and had a tea ceremony up in tree.

00:04:16.198 --> 00:04:17.214
- [Kelly] Oh my God.
(Nathan laughing)

00:04:17.214 --> 00:04:18.911
You are such a beautiful soul.

00:04:18.911 --> 00:04:20.070
- I'm making distance.

00:04:20.070 --> 00:04:22.170
- [Kelly] That was pretty
good comedic timing.

00:04:22.170 --> 00:04:23.780
- [Eric] (chuckling) We can go with that.

00:04:23.780 --> 00:04:25.280
- We can go with that. (laughing)

00:04:25.280 --> 00:04:26.550
I like that. (chuckling)

00:04:26.550 --> 00:04:27.383
What did you do?

00:04:27.383 --> 00:04:28.300
You've had enough time, sir.

00:04:28.300 --> 00:04:30.200
- Yes, I forgot all about it.
(crowd laughs)

00:04:30.200 --> 00:04:32.330
I had gone nearly a decade
without having a party,

00:04:32.330 --> 00:04:33.327
I had forgotten and someone said,

00:04:33.327 --> 00:04:35.430
"It's time, you have to have a party now."

00:04:35.430 --> 00:04:37.040
- Yeah, it's kind of stressful.

00:04:37.040 --> 00:04:38.610
- It can be, yes, yes, yes.

00:04:38.610 --> 00:04:39.443
But I had someone say,

00:04:39.443 --> 00:04:40.460
"I'll take care of all the arrangements."

00:04:40.460 --> 00:04:41.753
And I rented a restaurant,

00:04:41.753 --> 00:04:44.840
I had like 350 people there.

00:04:44.840 --> 00:04:46.257
Barbara Streisand showed up.

00:04:46.257 --> 00:04:47.718
(crowd applauds)

00:04:47.718 --> 00:04:48.551
(Melissa laughs)

00:04:48.551 --> 00:04:49.530
- Who also has my birthday.

00:04:49.530 --> 00:04:50.581
We're both April 24.
- What?

00:04:50.581 --> 00:04:51.490
- [Kelly] Don't worry about it.

00:04:51.490 --> 00:04:52.323
- Happy birthday, Barbara.

00:04:52.323 --> 00:04:53.930
- Yeah, happy birthday, Barbara.

00:04:53.930 --> 00:04:54.763
You and I,

00:04:54.763 --> 00:04:56.463
we're just birthday sisters.
(Mekia laughs)

00:04:56.463 --> 00:04:58.110
We have so much in common.
(Nathan laughing)

00:04:58.110 --> 00:04:58.943
That's amazing.

00:04:58.943 --> 00:05:00.040
Why did she randomly?

00:05:00.040 --> 00:05:02.569
- Her wonderful husband came
and played my father on Castle,

00:05:02.569 --> 00:05:03.566
I don't know if you remember that.

00:05:03.566 --> 00:05:04.399
- Yes.

00:05:04.399 --> 00:05:05.232
Do I remember?

00:05:05.232 --> 00:05:06.065
Yes.

00:05:06.065 --> 00:05:06.898
Still sexy as hell
- So he was invited,

00:05:06.898 --> 00:05:07.731
he brought along his lovely wife,

00:05:07.731 --> 00:05:08.770
and they both were there.

00:05:08.770 --> 00:05:09.603
It was really-

00:05:09.603 --> 00:05:10.811
- [Kelly] That's amazing.
(crowd cheers)

00:05:10.811 --> 00:05:11.644
- Right?

00:05:11.644 --> 00:05:12.477
We got on our thing.

00:05:12.477 --> 00:05:14.110
- I love that your dad
ended up being like,

00:05:14.110 --> 00:05:14.943
that was so amazing.

00:05:14.943 --> 00:05:16.540
Thanks again for coming, I'm so excited.

00:05:16.540 --> 00:05:17.423
- Thank you for having us.
(crowd cheers)

00:05:17.423 --> 00:05:18.556
- I'm so excited.
- Thank you.

00:05:18.556 --> 00:05:19.720
- I'm so excited you're all here.

00:05:19.720 --> 00:05:21.696
So what's been your favorite?

00:05:21.696 --> 00:05:22.529
Okay.

00:05:24.029 --> 00:05:26.090
It's amazing, the show, like it goes,

00:05:26.090 --> 00:05:27.240
and I love this about a show.

00:05:27.240 --> 00:05:28.620
I feel like you love this about shows too,

00:05:28.620 --> 00:05:29.830
'cause I've seen you in a lot of them.

00:05:29.830 --> 00:05:31.730
But it's so diverse,

00:05:31.730 --> 00:05:33.440
the show will touch on such emotional,

00:05:33.440 --> 00:05:35.270
I mean, the part where you
were like, almost died,

00:05:35.270 --> 00:05:37.863
and then the part with the
relationships, your ex,

00:05:40.511 --> 00:05:41.400
there's so many layers.

00:05:41.400 --> 00:05:42.350
Do y'all like that?

00:05:43.215 --> 00:05:45.970
I feel like writers on sets are on shows,

00:05:45.970 --> 00:05:48.030
don't always pay attention
to all the characters.

00:05:48.030 --> 00:05:49.210
I just wanna give a shout out,

00:05:49.210 --> 00:05:50.100
'cause the writers,

00:05:50.100 --> 00:05:51.864
it really is important that the writers,

00:05:51.864 --> 00:05:54.220
(hands clapping)
you really dive

00:05:54.220 --> 00:05:55.930
into all the characters,

00:05:55.930 --> 00:05:58.770
because you lose so
much opportunity there.

00:05:58.770 --> 00:06:00.260
And there's an individual story

00:06:00.260 --> 00:06:01.970
for each, whatever cultural background,

00:06:01.970 --> 00:06:03.180
or whatever's your gender.

00:06:03.180 --> 00:06:04.150
All of that.

00:06:04.150 --> 00:06:05.860
- I will say, I was always surprised.

00:06:05.860 --> 00:06:08.520
Like for example, she
was pregnant last year.

00:06:08.520 --> 00:06:10.160
And so she had a lot,

00:06:10.160 --> 00:06:13.380
they allowed her to
have a lot of days off.

00:06:13.380 --> 00:06:16.330
Yet her character's story
was still really big.

00:06:16.330 --> 00:06:18.750
You didn't didn't miss her at all.

00:06:18.750 --> 00:06:20.470
And they're really, really good with that.

00:06:20.470 --> 00:06:21.440
I don't know how they do that.

00:06:21.440 --> 00:06:23.560
When with such a large cast,

00:06:23.560 --> 00:06:26.160
how each character is equally important.

00:06:26.160 --> 00:06:26.993
- Yeah, yeah.

00:06:26.993 --> 00:06:28.280
I'm kind of smirking because my sister,

00:06:28.280 --> 00:06:29.300
and I had a full on conversation

00:06:29.300 --> 00:06:31.110
about how much we loved your
character pregnant. (chuckling)

00:06:31.110 --> 00:06:32.009
Your emotions.

00:06:32.009 --> 00:06:32.842
(Mekia laughs)

00:06:32.842 --> 00:06:34.690
It was like, "I love the writers
who are making you like."

00:06:34.690 --> 00:06:35.523
It's a really beautiful thing,

00:06:35.523 --> 00:06:36.830
you just said and
everybody was freaked out,

00:06:36.830 --> 00:06:37.835
'cause you were nice.

00:06:37.835 --> 00:06:38.820
(Kelly laughs)

00:06:38.820 --> 00:06:39.653
- Where else do you go?

00:06:39.653 --> 00:06:41.380
You can't go more negative with her,

00:06:41.380 --> 00:06:42.213
so they just-

00:06:42.213 --> 00:06:43.530
(Mekia laughs)
- [Kelly] No, it was amazing.

00:06:43.530 --> 00:06:45.000
It was so funny.

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:48.000
So Alyssa, so is there some
story about a banana peel?

00:06:48.000 --> 00:06:49.289
That's what I'm supposed to ask.

00:06:49.289 --> 00:06:50.122
- Oh.
- Yes.

00:06:50.122 --> 00:06:50.955
- So the banana peel story.

00:06:50.955 --> 00:06:54.270
So whenever Nathan has a banana,

00:06:54.270 --> 00:06:55.850
he grabs banana peel,

00:06:55.850 --> 00:06:58.100
and he throws it on the
floor, like a cartoon,

00:06:58.100 --> 00:06:59.310
like someone's gonna slip on it.

00:06:59.310 --> 00:07:00.890
But apparently I'm, I think,

00:07:00.890 --> 00:07:02.942
the only one he does it in front of.

00:07:02.942 --> 00:07:03.775
- I just-

00:07:03.775 --> 00:07:04.816
- Oh, you thought this
was a thing he does?

00:07:04.816 --> 00:07:05.649
- Yeah.
(Mekia laughing)

00:07:05.649 --> 00:07:06.482
- I just toss it on the floor.

00:07:06.482 --> 00:07:07.910
I go, "Hey, come here a second."

00:07:07.910 --> 00:07:09.490
And I put it between us.
(Kelly laughs)

00:07:09.490 --> 00:07:11.130
I go, "Hey, just come here a second."

00:07:11.130 --> 00:07:12.690
That's all, that's all I do.

00:07:12.690 --> 00:07:13.570
- Do you pick it up

00:07:13.570 --> 00:07:14.943
or does someone fall?
- Of course I pick it up.

00:07:14.943 --> 00:07:15.860
- No, he picks it up, he picks it up.

00:07:15.860 --> 00:07:17.138
- I was like, "What kind
of jack?" (laughing)

00:07:17.138 --> 00:07:19.600
(crowd laughs)
(Kelly laughing)

00:07:19.600 --> 00:07:21.640
Okay, before we go to break,

00:07:21.640 --> 00:07:23.800
I need to congratulate you on season five.

00:07:23.800 --> 00:07:24.870
- Thank you very much.

00:07:24.870 --> 00:07:27.154
(hands clapping)
(crowd cheering)

00:07:27.154 --> 00:07:28.990
- I loved y'all so much
for doing this show.

00:07:28.990 --> 00:07:30.930
I literally texted my producer.

00:07:30.930 --> 00:07:32.130
I was like, "Please get them on my show."

00:07:32.130 --> 00:07:33.304
And I love that it was for my birthday.

00:07:33.304 --> 00:07:34.137
- [Nathan] You know,

00:07:34.137 --> 00:07:34.970
something that's been
brought to our attention.

00:07:34.970 --> 00:07:37.282
You're no stranger to television work.

00:07:37.282 --> 00:07:38.997
We've seen your work.

00:07:38.997 --> 00:07:40.240
- Jesus.

00:07:40.240 --> 00:07:41.130
- [Nathan] Your acting work.

00:07:41.130 --> 00:07:42.640
- I hate acting.
(Mekia laughing)

00:07:42.640 --> 00:07:43.804
- On Sabrina the teenage witch.

00:07:43.804 --> 00:07:44.866
(Kelly laughs)

00:07:44.866 --> 00:07:45.930
- Wait, that was paying bills. (chuckling)

00:07:45.930 --> 00:07:47.700
- [Nathan] Can we go to the clip, please?

00:07:47.700 --> 00:07:48.700
- [Mekia] Roll the clip.

00:07:48.700 --> 00:07:50.654
- [Kelly] In my defense,
my roommate was an actor.

00:07:50.654 --> 00:07:51.628
- [Mekia] Oh there it is.

00:07:51.628 --> 00:07:52.461
- [Nathan] Here we go, here we go.

00:07:52.461 --> 00:07:53.294
Who's that?

00:07:53.294 --> 00:07:54.280
Who's that?

00:07:54.280 --> 00:07:55.113
- [Kelly] Yeah, that's me.

00:07:55.113 --> 00:07:56.823
(crowd applauds)

00:07:56.823 --> 00:07:58.465
You know what that is?

00:07:58.465 --> 00:08:00.839
That's fifty dollars. (chuckling)

00:08:00.839 --> 00:08:01.990
- [Nathan] First of all,
you're extremely talented,

00:08:01.990 --> 00:08:03.420
I love how you're looking
right down the barrel,

00:08:03.420 --> 00:08:04.317
right at the camera.

00:08:04.317 --> 00:08:05.150
(Melissa and Eric laughs)

00:08:05.150 --> 00:08:05.983
That's amazing.

00:08:05.983 --> 00:08:07.124
- I was supposed

00:08:07.124 --> 00:08:08.150
to be looking at her.
- That takes a lot of courage,

00:08:08.150 --> 00:08:08.983
that takes a lot of courage.

00:08:08.983 --> 00:08:10.290
- I was supposed to be looking at her.

00:08:10.290 --> 00:08:14.090
- But we think that if
you would do us the honor

00:08:14.090 --> 00:08:18.116
of taking some of that talent
and bringing it to our show.

00:08:18.116 --> 00:08:18.949
(crowd cheers)

00:08:18.949 --> 00:08:20.263
- Oh my God, are you serious?

00:08:20.263 --> 00:08:22.830
You guys, I'm a horrible actor.

00:08:22.830 --> 00:08:25.023
Can I just walk by and do this?

00:08:25.023 --> 00:08:25.930
(Mekia laughs)

00:08:25.930 --> 00:08:28.038
- We're gonna find you
something you're really good at.

00:08:28.038 --> 00:08:28.871
We're gonna find something.

00:08:28.871 --> 00:08:30.160
- Just have me playing Kelly Clarkson.

00:08:30.160 --> 00:08:32.138
I'm really, really bad at acting.

00:08:32.138 --> 00:08:32.971
(Nathan laughs)

00:08:32.971 --> 00:08:35.523
Okay, time, I'm sweating right now,

00:08:35.523 --> 00:08:37.604
but I'm totally in just so I can hang out.

00:08:37.604 --> 00:08:39.310
Time for another commercial break.

00:08:39.310 --> 00:08:40.600
Everybody, you can see The Rookie,

00:08:40.600 --> 00:08:43.350
Sundays on ABC or
streaming anytime on Hulu

00:08:43.350 --> 00:08:44.553
in my living room.

